<%# A field — or a pair of fields settled from one source — and what hangs off it: the
    text a model quoted as its source, chips that fill it, a hint for typing it. The
    field goes in the block, the rest in `attached`, one renderable or a list of them;
    blank entries drop out, so a caller may pass a render that produced nothing. The
    grouping itself is .field-group in application.css, not anything in this markup. %>
<%# locals: (attached: nil) %>
<% attachments = Array(attached).select(&:present?) %>
<div class="field-group">
  <%= yield %>
  <% if attachments.any? %>
    <div class="field-group__attached"><%= safe_join(attachments) %></div>
  <% end %>
</div>
